Subject: conf/settings.xml: on OpenVMS, a small default argLine for forked tests

surefire and failsafe fork the test JVM as a subprocess of Maven's JVM
(through MVNSH.EXE, which the launcher maps /bin/sh to). On OpenVMS a
subprocess draws on its job's pooled quotas, so both JVMs share one page
file quota, and with Java's default sizes the forked JVM failed to start
("Could not reserve enough space for object heap", "malloc failed",
"OutOfMemoryError: Metaspace") under a quota of about 250 MB (NOTES N12).

A profile activated by the OS family "openvms" sets the argLine property,
which surefire and failsafe use when the project sets no argLine, to a small
heap, the serial collector and a small code cache. Nothing changes on other
systems.

VMS-only, not for upstream.

--- a/conf/settings.xml	2026-11-06 21:08:01.073758160 +0000
+++ b/conf/settings.xml	2026-11-06 21:29:22.394679400 +0000
@@ -252,6 +252,24 @@
       </properties>
     </profile>
     -->
+
+    <!-- OpenVMS: a forked test JVM (surefire, failsafe) shares the page file
+         quota of Maven's own JVM, since a subprocess draws on its job's pooled
+         quotas; with the JVM's default sizes the second one cannot start.
+         This argLine keeps it small. A project that sets its own argLine
+         replaces it: add these options there, or raise PGFLQUOTA.
+         (vms-maven, docs/DECISIONS.md D5) -->
+    <profile>
+      <id>openvms</id>
+      <activation>
+        <os>
+          <family>openvms</family>
+        </os>
+      </activation>
+      <properties>
+        <argLine>-Xms8m -Xmx64m -XX:+UseSerialGC -XX:ReservedCodeCacheSize=16m</argLine>
+      </properties>
+    </profile>
   </profiles>
 
